Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Meridian Pedestrian Signal Drops Out
- Story & Context: At the intersection of 47th and Halsted, Reductus clamped a custom copper transformer onto the city's main lighting conduit, cutting the crosswalk power and triggering the first illegal Grid-Spit broadcast. As fifty spectators gathered in the freezing mist, the hacked traffic pole began pulsing a low 60Hz hum that matched the MC's opening tirade against municipal surveillance. A lone saxophone joined the rhythm, echoing down the empty avenue alongside a rhythmic, terrifying clanking of a pitch-shifted cowbell. "We spliced the city vein just to hear the dead pavement speak," Reductus bellowed over the cracked speaker horn, marking the official birth of the movement.
